  "answer": "### Summary of Coverage and Reimbursement for Lymphedema Supplies\n\nThe provided GRAPH CONTEXT outlines the coverage and reimbursement policies for lymphedema supplies under Medicare. The context includes the Authorizing Coverage Policy [DME-MAC-COPE147943], which specifies the requirements for coverage, including a documented diagnosis of lymphedema by a treating practitioner. The policy also outlines the necessary documentation for supplies, including the description of the base item, quantity to be dispensed, and the treating practitioner's signature.\n\nThe CMS Transmittal [TR-CR13286] and Enacted Public Law [PLAW-117-328] support the coverage policy, while the Federal Register Rule [REG-FR-2023-24455] codifies the changes to the Medicare program. The Regional Claims Contractor [JURIS-DME-B] and Beneficiary State [STATE-WI] are also specified in the context.\n\n### Covered Procedure Codes and Reimbursement Rates\n\nThe GRAPH CONTEXT lists several covered procedure codes for lymphedema compression treatment items, including [HCPCS-A6522], [HCPCS-A6520], [HCPCS-A6521], [HCPCS-A6523], [HCPCS-A6524], and [HCPCS-A6525]. The reimbursement rates for these codes are as follows:\n\n* [HCPCS-A6522]: Allowable Reimbursement = $290.47, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $58.09\n* [HCPCS-A6520]: Allowable Reimbursement = $119.54, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $23.91\n* [HCPCS-A6521]: Allowable Reimbursement = $474.33, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $94.87\n* [HCPCS-A6523]: Allowable Reimbursement = $689.17, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $137.83\n* [HCPCS-A6524]: Allowable Reimbursement = $362.39, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $72.48\n* [HCPCS-A6525]: Allowable Reimbursement = $731.60, Calculated 20% patient coinsurance = $146.32\n\nThese rates are specific to the state of Wisconsin and are based on the national fee schedule.",
